  "text": "\r\n<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN\" >\r\n<HTML>\r\n  <!--%@ OutputCache Duration=60 VaryByParam=\"flora_id;taxon_id\"  %-->\r\n\r\n<head>\r\n<!-- Google Tag Manager -->\r\n<script>(function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':\r\nnew Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],\r\nj=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src=\r\n'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);\r\n})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-TGK4SMV');</script>\r\n<!-- End Google Tag Manager -->\r\n<title>Ptychomitrium in Moss Flora of China @ efloras.org</title>\r\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href='/templates/eflora.css' />\r\n<script src=\"JavaScript/eflora.js\" type=\"text/javascript\" ></script>\r\n</head>\r\n\r\n\r\n  <!-- body onload=\"formMOMap.submit()\" -->\r\n  <body>\r\n\r\n    <TABLE id=\"TableMain\" cellSpacing=\"1\" cellPadding=\"1\" width=\"640\" border=\"0\">\r\n      <TR>\r\n        <TD><!--%@ Register TagPrefix=\"ucFlora\" TagName=\"TaxonSearchBox\" Src=\"TaxonSearchBox.ascx\" %-->\r\n\r\n<script language=\"javascript\">\r\n\r\nfunction jsClearTextBox(sender)\r\n{\r\n  // alert(formSearchBox[\"name_str\"].id);\r\n  // alert(sender.value);\r\n  if (sender.value == \"taxon name\")\r\n  {\r\n    sender.value = \"\";\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\n</script>\r\n<table id=\"ucEfloraHeader_tableHeaderWrapper\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"100%\" border=\"0\">\r\n\t<tr>\r\n\t\t<TD style=\"WIDTH: 479px\"><a id=\"ucEfloraHeader_linkFloraHome\" title=\"Flora Homepage\" href=\"flora_page.aspx?flora_id=4\"><img src=\"images/flora/eflora-logo-4.gif\" id=\"ucEfloraHeader_imageLogo\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Link to Moss Flora of China home\" /><br>\r\n        </a></TD>\r\n\t\t<TD valign=\"bottom\" align=\"right\">\r\n      <div id=\"ucEfloraHeader_panelSearchBox\">\r\n\t\t\t <!-- begin of search box -->\r\n        <FORM name=\"formSearchBox\" action=\"browse.aspx\" method=\"get\">\r\n          <TABLE borderColor=\"#ccffcc\" cellSpacing=\"0\" cellPadding=\"2\" width=\"200\" border=\"1\">\r\n            <TR>\r\n              <TD>\r\n                <span id=\"ucEfloraHeader_lblSearchBox\"><INPUT TYPE='Hidden' NAME='flora_id' ' id='flora_id' VALUE='4' >\n&nbsp;<input id=name_str name=name_str &nbsp;  value=''  class=small title='Use % as the wildcard\r\n(e.g. pinus % or pinus a%)'  onfocus='jsClearTextBox(this);' accessKey=s size=15> <input class=small type=submit value=Search name=btnSearch><br>\n <input name=chkAllFloras type=checkbox   > <span class=small>All Floras &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<A HREF='search_page.aspx?flora_id=4'  TARGET='_top'  class='a.link.small'>Advanced Search</A></span>\n</span></TD>\r\n            </TR>\r\n          </TABLE>\r\n        </FORM> <!-- end of search box -->\r\n      \r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    </TD>\r\n\t</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n</TD>\r\n      </TR>\r\n      <TR>\r\n        <TD id=\"tdSubHeader\">\r\n<table id=\"FooterTableOut\" width=\"100%\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td bgcolor=\"#999999\"><img src=\"~/images/layout/dot.gif\" alt=\"\" width=\"100%\" height=\"1\"></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <TD>\r\n      <table bgcolor=\"#ffffcc\" id=\"footerTable\" width=\"100%\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"2\" cellspacing=\"0\">\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td style=\"WIDTH: 291px\">Moss China V. 2 Page 251</td>\r\n          <TD align=\"right\">\r\n            <span id=\"ucEfloraSubHeader_lblLinks\"><a target='_top' href='/login.aspx'>Login</a>\n | <A HREF='/index.aspx'  TARGET='_top' >eFloras Home</A> | <A HREF='/help_page.aspx'  TARGET='_top' >Help</A></span></TD>\r\n        </tr>\r\n      </table>\r\n    </TD>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td bgcolor=\"#999999\"><img src=\"~/images/layout/dot.gif\" alt=\"\" width=\"100%\" height=\"1\"></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n</TD>\r\n      </TR>\r\n      <TR>\r\n        <TD id=\"tdBody\">\r\n          <table id=\"tableBody\" cellSpacing=\"0\" cellPadding=\"0\" width=\"100%\" border=\"0\">\r\n            <tr>\r\n              <td id=\"tdLeftBar\" valign=\"top\" width=\"0\"></td>\r\n\r\n              <td id=\"tdContent\" vAlign=\"top\" width=\"1930\">\r\n                <table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\">\r\n                  <tr>\r\n                    <td vAlign=\"top\">\r\n                      <table id=\"tableTaxonChain\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"1\" width=\"100%\" border=\"0\">\r\n\t<tr>\r\n\t\t<td><span id=\"lblTaxonChain\"><font size=\"2\"><A HREF='flora_page.aspx?flora_id=4'  TARGET='_top' \n\tTITLE='Flora homepage' >Moss China</A> | <A HREF='browse.aspx?flora_id=4'  TARGET='_top' >Family List</A> | <A HREF='volume_page.aspx?volume_id=4002&flora_id=4'  TARGET='_top' >Moss China V. 2</A> | <A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=10743'  TARGET='_top' >Ptychomitriaceae</A> <A HREF='browse.aspx?flora_id=4&start_taxon_id=10743'  TARGET='_top' \n\tTITLE='lower taxa' ><img border='0' src='images/layout/icon-list.gif'></A></font></span></td>\r\n\t</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n                      <P></P>\r\n                      <div id=\"panelTaxonTreatment\">\r\n\t\r\n                        <span id=\"lblTaxonDesc\"><!-- Default Template -->\r\n2. <b>Ptychomitrium</b> Fürnr., Flora.  12(2 Erg.):19.  1829.  \n<p>缩叶藓属  \r\n<P>\r\n\r\n<P>\r\n\r\n<P>\r\n<p>\r\n<p>\r\n\r\nPlants small to robust, green to yellowish green above, brown or black below, in loose or dense tufts. Stems erect or ascending, simple or branched; central strand well developed. Leaves often crisped or incurved, sometimes contorted when dry, erect-spreading to widely spreading when moist, lanceolate to linear-lanceolate or broadly lanceolate, sometimes keeled, concave above; margins erect or recurved, entire to strongly toothed above; costa single, strong, percurrent or ending below the apex; upper and median leaf cells small, rounded-quadrate to subquadrate, often bistratose, obscure, thick-walled, sometimes with sinuose walls; basal cells rectangular to elongate, thin-walled or with sinuose walls. Autoicous. Perigonia just below perichaetia. Perichaetial leaves not differentiated. Setae short to long, straight; capsules erect, symmetric, ovoid to oblong-ellipsoid, smooth; annuli none or well developed, consisting of thick-walled cells; peristome teeth 16, lanceolate to liner-lanceolate, deeply and irregularly splitting into 2–3 filiform, densely papillose segments; opercula with a short to long beak. Calyptrae mitrate, longitudinally plicate, lobed at the base, covering half to nearly the entire capsule. Spores spherical, coarsely to finely papillose or sometimes nearly smooth.<p>\r\n\r\nWijk et al. (1967, 1969) listed 87 species of Ptychomitrium in the world. Crosby et al. (2000) reduced this number to 54 species, 34 of which were given their highest confidence rating (four stars). T. Cao, C. Gao and Vitt (1995) recognized eight species in China. A new species, Ptychomitrium mamillose was recently published by S.-L. Guo et al. (2000) from Sichuan province.<p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<p>\r\n<p>\r\n\r\nThe distinguishing features of Ptychomitrium can be generalized as follows: 1) leaves often crisped or strongly incurved or contorted when dry; 2) calyptrae large, mitrate, covering a large portion of capsules, longitudinally plicate and lobed at the base; 3) peristome teeth haplolepideous, lanceolate to linear-lanceolate, irregularly splitting into 2–3 filiform, densely papillose segments; 4) costa single, strong, percurrent to subpercurrent; 5) the upper leaf cells rounded-quadrate to subquadrate, more or less thick-walled, smooth; and 6) the basal leaf cells elongate, thin-walled or with sinuose walls.<p>\r\n<p>\r\n<p>\r\n<P>\r\n</span>\r\n                        <P><!-- Key -->\r\n                        <div id=\"panelKey\">\r\n\t\t\r\n                          <BR clear=\"all\">\r\n                          <table id=\"tableKey\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"4\" width=\"100%\" border=\"0\">\r\n\t\t\t<tr bgcolor=\"#d5ffff\">\r\n\t\t\t\t<TD width=\"347\">\r\n                                <P>\r\n                                  <span id=\"lblKeyTitle\"><b><font size=\"2\"></font></b></span></P>\r\n                              </TD>\r\n\t\t\t\t<TD nowrap=\"nowrap\" align=\"right\">\r\n                                <P>\r\n                                  <span id=\"lblKeyEditLink\"><font size=\"1\"></font></span></P>\r\n                              </TD>\r\n\t\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t\t<tr bgcolor=\"#f1ffff\">\r\n\t\t\t\t<TD colspan=\"2\">\r\n                                <P>\r\n                                  <span id=\"lblKeyDesc\"><font size=\"2\"></font></span></P>\r\n                                <P>\r\n                                  <span id=\"lblKey\"><TABLE  WIDTH='100%' BORDER='0' >\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP><A NAME='KEY-1-1'>1</A></td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Upper leaf margins entire; calyptrae reaching the base of capsules; plants about 1 cm high</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP><A HREF='#KEY-1-2'>(2)</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP>+</td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Upper leaf margins serrate; calyptrae only reaching the middle of capsules; plants more than 2 cm high</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP><A HREF='#KEY-1-3'>(3)</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP><A NAME='KEY-1-2'>2</A> <A HREF='#KEY-1-1'>(1)</A></td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Leaves narrowly lanceolate from an ovate base, strongly concave and keeled above when moist; annuli absent</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP>2 <A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001254'  TARGET='_top' >Ptychomitrium fauriei</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP>+</td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Leaves oblong-lanceolate from a short, oblong base, plane or slightly incurved above when moist; annuli well developed</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP>7 <A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001258'  TARGET='_top' >Ptychomitrium sinense</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP><A NAME='KEY-1-3'>3</A> <A HREF='#KEY-1-1'>(1)</A></td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Leaves oblong-ovate to broadly lanceolate, obtuse to broadly acute at the apex</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP><A HREF='#KEY-1-4'>(4)</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP>+</td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Leaves linear-lanceolate to narrowly lanceolate from a broad base, acuminate to acute at the apex</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP><A HREF='#KEY-1-5'>(5)</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP><A NAME='KEY-1-4'>4</A> <A HREF='#KEY-1-3'>(3)</A></td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Leaves narrowly oblong-ovate to broadly lanceolate from a narrowly oblong base; peristome teeth divided into 2 long, subulate divisions; opercula with a short beak</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP>1 <A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001253'  TARGET='_top' >Ptychomitrium dentatum</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP>+</td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Leaves oblong-ovate from a wide, sub-ovate base; peristome teeth divided into three short divisions; opercula with a long beak</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP>9 <A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001261'  TARGET='_top' >Ptychomitrium wilsonii</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP><A NAME='KEY-1-5'>5</A> <A HREF='#KEY-1-3'>(3)</A></td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Median and basal leaf cells with sinuose, thick walls</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP><A HREF='#KEY-1-6'>(6)</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP>+</td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Median and basal leaf cells with straight, thin walls</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP><A HREF='#KEY-1-7'>(7)</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP><A NAME='KEY-1-6'>6</A> <A HREF='#KEY-1-5'>(5)</A></td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Upper part of leaves strongly contorted when dry, often secund when moist; median and basal leaf cells with strongly sinuose walls; annuli undifferentiated</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP>8 <A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001260'  TARGET='_top' >Ptychomitrium tortula</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP>+</td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Upper part of leaves crisped when dry, straight when moist; median and basal leaf cells with only somewhat sinuose walls; annuli well developed</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP>3 <A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001255'  TARGET='_top' >Ptychomitrium formosicum</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP><A NAME='KEY-1-7'>7</A> <A HREF='#KEY-1-5'>(5)</A></td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Leaves scarcely plicate at the base; upper part of leaves long, linear; plants 2-3 cm high</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP>5 <A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001256'  TARGET='_top' >Ptychomitrium linearifolium</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP>+</td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Leaves distinctly plicate at the base; upper part of leaves short, lanceolate; plants 3-5 cm high</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP><A HREF='#KEY-1-8'>(8)</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP><A NAME='KEY-1-8'>8</A> <A HREF='#KEY-1-7'>(7)</A></td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Upper and median leaf cells smooth; peristome 2-3 cleft to the base</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP>4 <A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=240002103'  TARGET='_top' >Ptychomitrium gardneri</A></td>\n</TR>\n<TR >\n  <td WIDTH=50 NOWRAP VALIGN=TOP>+</td>\n  <td WIDTH=400 VALIGN=TOP>Upper and median leaf cells bulging on the adaxial surfaces; peristome bifid to the base</td>\n  <td >&nbsp;</td>\n  <td VALIGN=TOP NOWRAP>6 <A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=240002104'  TARGET='_top' >Ptychomitrium mamillosum</A></td>\n</TR>\n</TABLE>\n</span></P>\r\n                              </TD>\r\n\t\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t\t<tr bgcolor=\"#d5ffff\">\r\n\t\t\t\t<TD colspan=\"2\">\r\n                                <span id=\"lblKeyList\"><font size=\"2\"></font></span></TD>\r\n\t\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t</table>\r\n\t\t\r\n                        \r\n\t</div></P> \r\n                        <P>\r\n                          <span id=\"lblLowerTaxonList\"><p>\n<B>Lower Taxa</B><br>\n<ul>\n<li><A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001253' \n\tTITLE='Accepted Name' ><b>Ptychomitrium</b> <b>dentatum</b>  (Mitt.) Jaeg.</A><li><A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001254' \n\tTITLE='Accepted Name' ><b>Ptychomitrium</b> <b>fauriei</b>  Besch.</A><li><A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001255' \n\tTITLE='Accepted Name' ><b>Ptychomitrium</b> <b>formosicum</b>  Broth. & Yas.</A><li><A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=240002103' \n\tTITLE='Accepted Name' ><b>Ptychomitrium</b> <b>gardneri</b>  Lesq.</A><li><A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001256' \n\tTITLE='Accepted Name' ><b>Ptychomitrium</b> <b>linearifolium</b>  Reim.</A><li><A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=240002104' \n\tTITLE='Accepted Name' ><b>Ptychomitrium</b> <b>mamillosum</b>  S.-L. Guo, T. Cao & C. Gao</A><li><A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001258' \n\tTITLE='Accepted Name' ><b>Ptychomitrium</b> <b>sinense</b>  (Mitt.) Jaeg.</A><li><A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001260' \n\tTITLE='Accepted Name' ><b>Ptychomitrium</b> <b>tortula</b>  (Harv.) Jaeg.</A><li><A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=4&taxon_id=200001261' \n\tTITLE='Accepted Name' ><b>Ptychomitrium</b> <b>wilsonii</b>  Sull. & Lesq.</A></ul>\n<p>\n</span></P>\r\n                        <BR clear=\"all\">\r\n                        <P>&nbsp;</P>\r\n                        \r\n                        <P></P>\r\n                      \r\n</div>\r\n                      <P><div id=\"panelTaxonLinks\">\r\n\t&nbsp;</P>\r\n                      <P>\r\n                        <table id=\"tableLinkList\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"4\" width=\"100%\" border=\"1\">\r\n\t\t<tr bgcolor=\"#ffffcc\">\r\n\t\t\t<TD><span id=\"lblLinkTitle\"><font size=\"2\"><b>Related Links</b> (opens in a new window)</font></span></TD>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<TD>\r\n                              <P><span id=\"lblLinkList\"><b>Treatments in Other Floras @ www.efloras.org</b><ul>\n<li><A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=3&taxon_id=127592'  TARGET='_top' \n\tTITLE='treatment in Chinese Plant Names' >Chinese Plant Names</A><li><A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=1&taxon_id=127592'  TARGET='_top' \n\tTITLE='treatment in Flora of North America' >Flora of North America</A></ul>\n<p>\n<b>Other Databases</b>\n<ul>\n\n<li><A HREF='http://mobot.mobot.org/cgi-bin/search_pick?name=Ptychomitrium'  TARGET='FLORA_LINK' \n\tTITLE='W3TROPICOS' >W<SUP>3</SUP>TROPICOS</A>\n<li><A HREF='http://www.ipni.org/ipni/IpniServlet?family=&infrafamily=&genus=Ptychomitrium&infragenus=&species=&infraspecies=&author_abbrev=&publication_title=&is_apni_record=on&is_gci_record=on&is_ik_record=on&